File/source list
Each row should show file name, type, source, last modified time, last indexed time, processing state, project/collection, permissions and error details. Provide search/filter/sort and pagination. Provide a clear distinction between available in Drive, selected for LORIN, downloaded, indexed and available for retrieval.
States
Every view must implement loading, empty, connected, partial sync, syncing, paused, failed, reauthorization, disconnected and offline states. Do not display green Connected simply because a token record exists. Perform an actual lightweight authenticated status check.
B10. Data lifecycle and owner controls
Implement separate, explicit actions:
- Remove from index: remove LORIN chunks/embeddings and mark source unselected while leaving the original Drive file untouched.
- Disconnect Google: stop sync, revoke/retire tokens as appropriate, stop/expire channels, retain or delete already indexed data according to the owner's explicit choice.
- Delete LORIN copy: remove stored downloaded originals, extracted text, chunks and embeddings under the configured retention policy.
- Delete from Google Drive: not part of the initial release; if ever added, require separate explicit confirmation and verify Drive write permission.
Never delete or modify the original Google Drive document as a side effect of removing it from LORIN.
