B14. Acceptance tests — required before completion
OAuth and account
- Owner can connect the intended Google account.
- State/CSRF validation blocks invalid callbacks.
- The backend exchanges the authorization code successfully.
- Refresh token is encrypted and never reaches the browser.
- Granted scopes are verified and shown accurately.
- Reauthorization works after revocation/expiry.
- Disconnect removes/invalidates stored credentials and stops jobs safely.
Picker and permissions
- Picker opens with the restricted key and correct project App ID.
- Owner can select an accessible supported file.
- Cancellation leaves the connection unchanged.
- Selected file is accessible through Drive API.
- Folder child enumeration is tested and based on actual canListChildren.
- Inaccessible files are reported, not silently skipped as successful.
Content and knowledge
- PDF, DOCX, TXT, CSV, XLSX, PPTX and supported Workspace exports are processed.
- Unsupported/oversized/malformed files are rejected safely.
- File is indexed exactly once under duplicate retries.
- LORIN can answer a test question from a selected document with a correct citation.
- Retrieval respects owner/project/source permissions.
Incremental sync
- New file selected and indexed.
- Existing file modified and reindexed.
- Rename/move updates metadata.
- Removed/trashed/inaccessible source is tombstoned and excluded from current retrieval.
- Duplicate webhook notifications do not create duplicate work.
- Pagination and multiple change pages are handled.
- Token refresh and interrupted sync recover safely.
- Reconciliation catches a missed webhook.
Privacy and deletion
- Unselected documents are never imported in selected-file mode.
- No refresh token or client secret exists in frontend bundles, browser storage, source control or logs.
- Private/local-only content is not sent to public LLMs.
- Removing a source from the LORIN index does not delete the original Drive file.
- Delete/export/recovery policies behave as documented.
UI/UX
- Every button works.
- Every status maps to real backend state.
- Progress comes from actual job records.
- Errors identify the failed file and recovery action.
- Desktop, tablet and mobile layouts work.
- Accessibility and keyboard navigation pass.
B15. Release gates
Gate 1 — Owner configuration: APIs, consent screen, OAuth client, Picker key, origins and redirect URI configured.

Gate 2 — Secure connection: Real OAuth connection, encrypted token storage and verified account status work.

Gate 3 — Selected file ingestion: Picker-selected file downloads/exports, parses and indexes correctly.

Gate 4 — Knowledge retrieval: LORIN answers with accurate, permission-filtered citations.

Gate 5 — Synchronization: Incremental changes, deletions, recovery and reconciliation pass.

Gate 6 — Production readiness: Verification, privacy review, operational monitoring and security tests pass.

A gate cannot be marked complete because UI exists. Attach test evidence and describe the exact account, scopes and file types tested (without exposing personal file contents or tokens).
